  "title": "Minimal graphs with a prescribed number of spanning trees",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Let $n \\geq 3$ be an integer and let $\\alpha(n)$ denote the least integer $k$ such that there exists a simple graph on $k$ vertices having precisely $n$ spanning trees. Then $\\alpha(n) = o(\\log{n}).$",
